window.docContents[106].resolve({"/Extensivity/Aggregating-about-a-shared-parameter/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--Aggregating-about-a-shared-parameter":{"contents":"Some quantities add only relative to something the parts must share — a moment of inertia about\na common axis, an energy about a common datum. A Measurement reads a carving and nothing else,\nso the parameter is made an explicit argument; what that buys is not a weaker law but a statable\none, about the case a library that forgets the axis actually hits.\n\nThe parameter is kind-specific — an axis for a moment of inertia, a frame for a momentum, a\nreference point for an angular momentum — and the transports relating two parameter values\nform a tower: each correction is priced in a summary that is itself extensive one rung down,\ngrounding out in mass. The worked witness is a rover (RoverExtensivity, examples): whether\nits four wheels' spins, each read about its own axle, may be summed against the chassis is\ndecided by the priced correction — each assembly's momentum — which vanishes parked and does\nnot while driving.\n\nA kind is extensive about a parameter when fixing the parameter — an axis, an origin, a datum\n— makes the ordinary additivity law hold. This is extensivity at\nevery parameter at once, not a weakening of it, which is what makes the mixed-parameter\nstatement a claim about the predicate rather than about one lucky choice.\n\nRealized as ExtensiveAbout k m over a ParamMeasurement, with ExtensiveAbout.at recovering\nExtensive k (m a) at each parameter so both §13.5 capstones apply unchanged. Its companion\nTransports carries the correction as an argument rather than defining it as the difference: a\ntransport law is useful only when the correction is computable from data the part already\ncarries.\n\nThe parallel-axis theorem, over any carving. The moment of inertia about  is the moment\nabout  plus a correction built from the carving's own first moment and total mass,\n\nBoth summaries are themselves extensive over the same carving, which is why this is a\nmetrological statement and not only an algebraic identity: transporting an aggregate costs\nonly quantities the parts already carry. Taking  at the centre of mass kills the first\nmoment and leaves the textbook . Builds on extensivity\nabout a parameter.\n\nBy induction on the carving: at a leaf it is ring normalization of\n, and at a join the three folds distribute. The\nInt ring arithmetic is why it lives in the Mathlib-backed AggregationLaws rather than the\ncore. What the core exhibits is the failure it corrects: two point masses read about axes\nthrough themselves contribute nothing each, where the rod about its centre reads 2.\n\nA momentum transports between frames, priced in mass. The momentum read in the frame at\n is the momentum read at  plus the carving's mass times the frame difference,\n\nThe parameter of extensivity about a parameter is a frame here\nrather than an axis, and the failure it prices is reading each part in its own rest frame:\nevery reading is zero, so the untransported sum reports a system with no momentum at all.\n\nBy induction on the carving: ring at a leaf on , folds\ndistributing at a join. The core exhibits the failure (drift_rest_frames_wrong: two drifting\nmasses read 0 in their own rest frames where the laboratory reads the pair at 3) and\ndrift_rest_frames_corrected closes the gap from the general law, with the two corrections\nbeing the parts' own laboratory momenta.\n\nAn angular momentum transports between reference points, priced in momentum. Componentwise\nover any carving,\n\nwith the momentum components entering as the first moments of the velocities. This is the\nmiddle rung of the transport tower: inertia's correction is priced\nin mass and first moment, this one in momentum, and momentum's in\nmass — each price itself extensive one rung down, so mixed-parameter aggregation is checkable\nall the way to the ground.\n\nBy induction on the carving, ring at a leaf. Taking  at a part's own mass centre and\n at the system's shows the spin/orbital split of an angular momentum is this law and not\na new principle, and a part whose momentum vanishes reads the same about every point. The\nrover instantiates both readings: each wheel's spin reads 2 about its own axle, parked or\ndriving; parked, every assembly's momentum vanishes and the four spins sum against the\nchassis unchanged, while driving each transport costs −15 and the untransported sum misses\nthe whole by exactly the four prices.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Extensivity","header":"13.4. Aggregating about a shared parameter","id":"/Extensivity/Aggregating-about-a-shared-parameter/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--Aggregating-about-a-shared-parameter"},"/ISO-80000-4-___-Mechanics/Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-kind-does-___-the-torque___energy-case/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--ISO-80000-4-___-Mechanics--Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-kind-does-___-the-torque___energy-case":{"contents":"Part 4 holds the textbook example of a dimension collision. Torque (moment of force,\n4-12.1/4-12.2) and energy (work, 4-28) are both M·L²·T⁻² — yet they are distinct\nkinds, measured in distinct units: the newton metre is reserved for torque, the joule for\nenergy, precisely because they are different kinds. And Part 4 is dense with such\ncollisions: momentum and impulse (M·L·T⁻¹); angular momentum, angular impulse, and\naction (M·L²·T⁻¹); pressure, stress, and the three elastic moduli (M·L⁻¹·T⁻²); and a\nwhole dimension-one family — the relative densities, the strains, the Poisson number, the\nfriction factors, the drag coefficient, and the efficiency.\n\n\n\nTorque is not energy, though both are M·L²·T⁻². There exist distinct ISO 80000-4 kinds\nwith the same dimension — torque and energy witness it. No dimension-only type system can\nseparate them; the kind layer does. This is the textbook case that a dimension does not\nclassify a quantity. Uses the dimension map.\n\niso80000_4_dim_collision : ∃ a b : DimensionedKind, a.kind ≠ b.kind ∧ a.dim = b.dim,\nwitnessed by ⟨torque, mechanicalEnergy, …⟩ with torque_ne_energy (a decide) and\nreflexivity. The companion momentum_ne_impulse is the M·L·T⁻¹ case. Axiom-free.\n\nA newton metre is not a joule, though both are M·L²·T⁻². The SI units of torque and\nenergy are not commensurable, because their kinds differ — the unit-level form of the\ntorque/energy collision, a type-level fact the dimension cannot see. Uses\nmetrological units.\n\nnewtonMetre_joule_not_commensurable : ¬ newtonMetre.Commensurable joule by unfolding to\nthe underlying kinds and decide (torque's kind differs from the energy kind).\n\nThe dimension-1 disambiguation, on the standard. There exist distinct ISO 80000-4 kinds\nwith the same dimension one — efficiency and the relative mass density witness it,\nalongside the strains, the Poisson number, and the friction factors. Dimension cannot\nseparate them; the kind layer does. Uses the dimension map.\n\niso80000_4_dim_one_collision : ∃ a b : DimensionedKind, a.kind ≠ b.kind ∧ a.dim = b.dim\n∧ a.dim = 1, witnessed by ⟨efficiency, relativeMassDensity, …⟩ with\nefficiency_ne_relativeMassDensity (a decide) and reflexivity. Axiom-free.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009ISO 80000-4 — Mechanics","header":"20.3. Dimension does not classify; the kind does — the torque/energy case","id":"/ISO-80000-4-___-Mechanics/Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-kind-does-___-the-torque___energy-case/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--ISO-80000-4-___-Mechanics--Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-kind-does-___-the-torque___energy-case"}});